  "prediction": "The report outlines recommendations for the Internal Revenue Service (IRS) and the Department of the Treasury to improve the processing of taxpayer appeals. The IRS is encouraged to conduct a skills gap analysis, address collection staff transfer deficiencies, establish timeframes and monitoring procedures for examination compliance units, and report data on appeal request times to each compliance unit. The Department of the Treasury should make Appeals customer service standards and performance more transparent to the public and develop a mechanism for soliciting public input on appeal policies and procedures. The report also notes that the IRS and Treasury agreed with the recommendations and will provide detailed corrective action plans.",
  "scored_prediction": "The report outlines recommendations for the Internal Revenue Service (IRS) and the Department of the Treasury to improve the processing of taxpayer appeals. The IRS is encouraged to conduct a skills gap analysis, address collection staff transfer deficiencies, establish timeframes and monitoring procedures for examination compliance units, and report data on appeal request times to each compliance unit. The Department of the Treasury should make Appeals customer service standards and performance more transparent to the public and develop a mechanism for soliciting public input on appeal policies and procedures. The report also notes that the IRS and Treasury agreed with the recommendations and will provide detailed corrective action plans.",
